hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3006","Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa, narrated to us Jarir, on the authority of 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, on the authority of 'Ata', who said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he mentioned the hadith, saying:

""Then he (ﷺ) turned to the corners of the House (the Ka'bah) and faced each corner, saying the takbir (Allah is the Greatest), tahil (there is no god but Allah), tahmid (all praise is for Allah), and made supplications and sought forgiveness from Allah.""

And he (Jarir) mentioned the rest of the hadith.

**CHAPTER:**"
